[[1024,127,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               monitors\nand controls the entire electronic injection system.</p><p>The supply for the engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10\nis controlled by the ignition (15/54) at pin 28 by the line protected\nby fuse F4 of the additional fuse box B98A.</strong></p><p>The relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls the  system\nsupply: it is supplied by the battery, from the line for maxifuse\nEFI of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; pin 72 of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 sends the enablement\nsignal which excites relay J10 and sends power to the control unit,\ndirectly to pin 5 and, via the line of fuse F3 of the additional\nfuse box B98A, to pin 1.</strong></p><p>The relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J15 is also supplied by the\nbattery, from the  line for maxifuse EFI of B99; pin 91 of control\nunit M10 sends the signals which energize the relay, which provides\nthe supply to the fuel pump N40, which is connected to earth through\nthe inertia switch I50.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               In case of  impact, this cuts off the\ncircuit to prevent the danger of fuel delivery. Pins 2, 4 and 6 of\nconnector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 are earthed.</strong></p><p>The diesel preheating relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J17 is supplied\nby the battery via the line protected by the GLOW maxifuse of B99\nor fuse B39, and controls the operation of the diesel heating resistor\nO20;</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               a signal from the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 (from pin 68) deactivates\nthe system once heating has taken place.</strong></p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , responsible for\ncontrolling preheating of heater plugs \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , is supplied directly\nby the battery via a line protected by the GLOW maxifuse of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .\nIt is supplied - connector C - by the line of fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2 of the\nadditional fuse box B98A, and exchanges the command and control\nsignals with pins 52 and 93 of M10 which controls the timer.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               Connector\nB is connected to the heater plugs \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A40.</strong></p><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\nsignals from the various sensors in order to monitor all engine\nservice conditions.</p><p>Rpm sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K46 supplies information on\nengine speed via a frequency signal sent to pins 12 and 27 of connector\nB of control unit M10.</strong></p><p>Timing sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K47 is supplied from pin\n11 of connector B of control unit M10.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               It receives a reference\nearth from pin 20 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 and sends\nit a signal of frequency corresponding to the timing of pin 50 of\nthe same connector.</strong></p><p>The engine temperature sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K45, receives\na reference earth from pin 41 of the control unit M10 and supplies\na signal proportional to the temperature of the engine coolant to\npin 58 of connector B.</strong></p><p>The air flow meter \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives a\ngeneral power supply from the line of fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; a reference earth is received from pin 44 of\nconnector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               It is supplied by the control unit from\npin 29 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10, and sends pin 42 of connector B\na signal proportional to the air flow.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               There is also an air\ntemperature sensor inside \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K41 which sends an air temperature\nsignal to pin 37 of connector B of M10.</strong></p><p>Accelerator pedal K55 is fitted with two\nbuilt-in potentiometers (a main one and a safety back-up). The former\nreceives power and earth from pins 30 and 45,  respectively of connector\nA of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 and sends a corresponding signal to pin 9.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               The latter\nreceives power and earth from pins 46 and 8, respectively of connector\nA of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 and sends a signal to pin 31.</strong></p><p>The fuel temperature sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K81</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               measures\nthe temperature of the diesel entering. It receives a reference\nearth from pin 10 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 and sends the fuel temperature\nsignal to pin 11.</strong></p><p>The supercharging sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K82 measures\nthe pressure and temperature in the intake chamber, downstream of\nthe turbocharger.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               It is supplied from pin 13 of connector B\nof \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 and receives a reference earth from pin 23 of connector\nB.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               The signal corresponding to the pressure value is sent to\npin 40 of connector B of the control unit. There is also an air\ntemperature sensor inside \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K82 which sends a signal to pin 53\nof connector B of M10.</strong></p><p>The fuel pressure sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K83</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is responsible\nfor providing the injection control unit with a feedback signal\nfor governing pressure and injection duration. It receives power\nand a reference earth from pins 28 and 8 respectively of connector\nB of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10;</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               it then sends the pressure signal to pin 43.</p><p>The fuel pressure regulator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N77</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               has\nthe task of keeping the value of the fuel pressure in the accumulator\nconstant. The two control signals come from pins 4 and 34 of connector\nB of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10.</strong></p><p>The EGR solenoid \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls exhaust\ngas recirculation.  it receives a supply from the line for fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2\nof the additional fuse box B98A;</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , and is controlled by a signal\nfrom pin 60 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10.</strong></p><p>The turbine variable geometry control solenoid \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L36 governs the operation of the turbine in accordance with engine\nload; it is supplied by the line of fuse F2 of the additional fuse\nbox B98A and is controlled by a signal from pin 7 of connector A\nof M10.</strong></p><p>The solenoid valve on the throttle casing \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L62\nshutters and closes the throttle, for example when the engine is\nswitched off;</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                                it receives a supply from the line for fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2\nof the additional fuse box B98A;</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and is controlled by a signal\nfrom pin 59 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10.</strong></p><p>The engine management control unit sends\nthe command to the injectors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N70 from pins 16-47, 2-31, 1-46,\n17-33 and 18-48 of connector B of M10 for cylinders 1, 2, 3 , 4\nand 5, respectively.</strong></p><p>Pin 59 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 receives the signal coming\nfrom the brake lights switch I30, with the supply controlled by\nthe ignition (INT) from fuse F1 of the junction unit B1 or, depending\non the version, from fuse F4 of the additional fuse box B98 B.</strong></p><p>Pin 79 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 receives an earth signal\ncoming from the clutch pedal switch I31.</strong></p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 - pins 61 and 62 - communicates\nwith ABS control unit  M50 via the CAN line: this line, on versions\nwith VDC, passes through steering sensor K58 and reaches ABS control\nunit M50.</strong></p><p>The speedometer module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10 receives a\nsupply controlled by the ignition (INT) from the line protected\nby fuse F4 of the additional fuse box B98B; when the earth signal\narrives from pin 71 of connector A of M10, the &#x27;EOBD&#x27; warning light\ncomes on.</strong></p><p>The rev counter  module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15 also receives\na supply controlled by the ignition (INT) from the line protected\nby fuse F4 of the additional fuse box B98B; when the earth signal\narrives from pin 92 of connector A of M10, the &#x27;heater plugs&#x27; warning\nlight comes on.</strong></p><p>The coolant temperature signal is sent to\nthe auxiliary instrument from pin 94 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 \n\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE4023\n\t\tDASHBOARD CENTRE AUXILIARY EQUIPMENT()\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 .</strong></p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 is connected to the\nALFA ROMEO CODE control unit M20 via a line from pin 47 of connector\nA;</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               in this way if the ALFA ROMEO CODE unit does not detect a\ncorrect code, it does not issue enablement and the engine is not\nstarted.</p><p>The control unit is equipped with a self-diagnostic\nunit that may be used by connecting the unit to connector R10 via\npin 25 of connector A.</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 sends from pin 48 of\nconnector A, a signal proportional to the engine rpm\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE4020\n\t\tREV COUNTER INSTRUMENT\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 ;</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               a consumption\nsignal leaves pin 27 of connector A for the speedometer \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234310\">E4021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 is connected with\nthe air conditioning system through pins 29 and 54.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               This makes\nit possible to adjust the engine idle speed as the load increases\neach time the compressor is switched on or to switch off the compressor\nin the case of high engine speed or load conditions \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234652\">E6021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit also controls the engine\ncooling system: pins 69, 42, 81 and 90 control the engagement of\nthe relevant fans \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234439\">E5020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Cruise control \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234591\">E5060</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              function\nmanagement signals leave pins 80, 49, 77, 78, 56 and 38 of connector\nA of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10.</strong></p>"]]